16	doc.push(P("This was left open deliberately. The sentences carrying these numbers are also the document's defence against a flat-tier cliff objection, and D08 already labels them a pricing hypothesis validated only against modelled return. Restating them at 1.77×/3.36× on the A2/D08 cost basis — which is the basis the rate card itself prices on — is defensible; so is stating the frame. That is a commercial decision about what the first real conversation opens with, and it changes a client-facing sentence in two documents — so it should be decided, not quietly edited. Both answers are costed in the decision paper, §6–§7."));
17	
18	doc.push(H2("2. Finding 2 — D08's modelled benefits exceed what A1 produces, and the cause is now identified"));
19	doc.push(P("D08 §5 says a 500-axle customer sees $6–8M of avoided damage in the pilot year and $14–20M over four years; §6 says $40–60M over six years with a 20×–30× return. A1 at 500 axles with its default assumptions produces $696,675 net annual benefit. The ratio is between 5× and 14× across the three periods."));
20	doc.push(P("The cause is a modelling fork, not an arithmetic error, and it is now traced. Two different figures for the probability that a missed defect escalates to a catastrophic event exist in the repository:"));
21	doc.push(table(
22	  ["Location", "Probability", "Expected cost per missed defect"],
23	  [
24	    ["backend/roi.py — P_CATASTROPHIC_GIVEN_MISSED_DEFECT", "2%", "$29,065,000"],
