576	  "The first audit found five. The no_regression fix had landed in backend/ledger_export.py but not in tools/verify_ledger_export.py — the very tool D09 §4.5.4 names for the quarterly check — so the contract's own verifier rejected every legitimate chained full export while the in-repo one passed. inspect() never opened a bundle, so a record edited inside a signed bundle came back 'series is continuous'. It could not see a missing period at all. A lost series.json silently restarted the series under a docstring promising refusal, and the test asserting it did so was named as though it tested the opposite. Concurrent runs stranded signed bundles the state never recorded. The second audit then found four more. The period walker HUNG FOREVER on a 53-week ISO year — 2026 is one — so the quarterly tool would simply never return. The same walker could not see a deleted latest month. due_exports read the state outside the lock, so concurrent run_due calls produced duplicate bundles the cadence says must not exist. And the test written to guard the verifier fix asserted that a string was absent in a way that passed when the check was deleted entirely — a test that could not fail. That last one is the most instructive: it was written immediately after an audit about checks that pass for the wrong reason, and it repeated the error in miniature.",
577	  { fill: "FBEAEA", labelColor: RED },
578	));
